# Deeeep UI basics

Every new or changed UI element must meet these rules. Check them before finishing any task.

## Cursors
- Pointing hand (`NSCursor.pointingHand`) on every clickable custom control: buttons, icon buttons, mode gauges, the − and + of the pomodoro stepper, ••• menus, push-back icons, disclosure chevrons, header icons (History, Tour, trash).
- I-beam on editable text. Open hand over movable rows (not over the name, which keeps the arrow until it is edited) and closed hand while dragging.
- Disabled or display-only elements keep the arrow cursor.
- Standard `NSMenu` items and system controls keep their system cursors.

## Hover and states
- Every clickable custom control has a subtle hover state (e.g. a rounded background at white 6%, radius 6).
- Icon-only buttons: square 28×28 pt hit area with the icon centered. The hover/pressed background fills the square (radius 6). Round controls get a 28 pt circular hover. The icon size and the layout never change.
- Disabled: 40% opacity, no hover, a tooltip explaining why when that's useful.
- Clicking a custom control never takes keyboard focus; focus rings only for keyboard navigation.
- Hover must never shift the layout (no size or padding changes).

## Tooltips and accessibility
- Every icon-only control has a tooltip and an accessibility label.
- Custom controls expose the right accessibility role, and a hint when the click action isn't obvious.

## Layout
- The window is at least 450×550. Every element must fit there with nothing clipped.
- In rows, only the task name truncates (trailing "…"). Times, counts, and icons never truncate.
- Numbers and times use monospaced digits so they line up.
- Keep existing spacing, font sizes, and colors. Reuse existing components instead of new styling.

## Row grid
- All list rows (Queue, LATER, Done, History) start with the gauge column (28 pt: 20 pt gauge + 8 pt gap) and a name that takes the rest of the row. An essential value may sit at the right edge. Names truncate with a trailing "…".
- Same column = same meaning. Never place a different kind of value in a column.
- Tag column is decided per list: queue, LATER, Done, and History (one list across all days). A list with at least one tagged row gives every row, untagged ones included, the column between gauge and name: widest tag label in that list plus 8 pt, clamped to 28–60 pt (a longer tag ends in "…"). A list without tags has no column and no empty space. Lists never share a width. It updates live with a 150 ms slide (instant with Reduce Motion); a held row uses the layout of the list it is over. Only a tagged row drops its column while its name is edited.
- Tags are plain text, never controls (no pointing hand, hover, tooltip or menu). Colors `Theme.tag1`…`tag6` are automatic and cannot be changed. Old muted-prefix size: 11 pt regular, small caps, 0.04 em tracking, 6 pt to the name; 60% in Done and History. Plain text in the menu bar and in the edit field.
- Current task in its own NOW section (not draggable) above TODO: a NOW header (label only, no stats, chip or icons), the row styled as the running row (bgCardActive, 3 pt bar in the mode color, gauge at 50% with the drifting wave). The name and tag use exactly the list rows' font, size and weight (13 pt name, 11 pt tag, regular); never a larger or bolder text for the current task, then a 1 pt `lineSubtle` divider with 12 pt above and below. Idle and break have no NOW section and no divider. TODO rows are always movable; the current task is not in the TODO list but stays first in the queue.
- Paused = desaturated and still, never badged: the tank (air, water, back wave and crest, digits and pause glyph, text, scale) and the NOW row (bar, gauge, name `#B9CDD1`, tag at 60%) turn grey in a 400 ms crossfade (instant with Reduce Motion). Waves frozen, water level unchanged. The Resume pill keeps its mode (or sand) color. No chip, badge or "Paused" text.
- Running and next markers: a 3 pt bar at the left edge of the card, clipped by the card's rounded corners (a clipped overlay, as in `RowCard`). Mode surface color at 100% (running) or 40% (next). Not a crescent, capsule, or border.
- Right-side order: finish time (hover) · ••• (hover) · stepper (count at rest when ≠ 1). The stepper is always the rightmost element; the count's x position never changes. Done and History: finish time (hover) · ↩ (hover) · worked time · `×n`, with `×n` at the same x as the queue's count.
- Count = fixed 72 pt stepper slot with its right edge 10 pt from the card edge (••• 4 pt left of it); − and + appear on hover; the number never moves. Done and History show a display-only `×n` in the same slot position.
- Reserve only what is visible at rest. Queue and LATER at count 1 show nothing on the right, so the name runs to the row's 10 pt right padding; any other count shows only `×n` at the center of the stepper slot (46 pt from the card edge) and the name ends 8 pt before it. The hover cluster (finish time, •••, − ×n +) is an overlay with the hover background and a 24 pt left fade; it never changes the name's frame, and the count number stays at the same x. Done and History keep the worked time and `×n` in fixed columns; the name ends before them.
- Queue and LATER rows are cards without dividers. Done and History rows are flat without dividers.
- While a row's name is edited, its stepper, ••• and finish-time overlay fade out (120 ms) and the field runs to the row's right padding; they return when editing ends.
- Rows show only the essentials at rest (gauge, name, non-default values). Secondary values and row actions appear on hover.
- Hover controls appear as a right-aligned overlay with a 24 pt left fade. The gauge and name start never move. Names truncate with "…".
- Every hover-only action is also reachable by right-click (context menu), keyboard, and VoiceOver.
- A count of 1 is the default and is not shown at rest.

## Section headers
- Left-aligned, uppercase 11 pt medium label plus muted stats. Header icons sit in the Action column.
- Numbers use SF Pro with monospaced digits, never SF Mono.

## Motion
- Animations are short (150–300 ms) and play once. Never a second "catch-up" animation.
- Lists use stable ids. Reordering animates as a move, never remove + insert.
- Rows drag from anywhere (gauge, tag, name, empty space) after 4 pt of movement; only the −/+ and ••• hover controls never start a drag. A click without movement keeps its normal action (gauge click cycles the mode on mouse up).
- Queue and LATER are one drag area. While a row is held, LATER opens with every day as a drop target, and the row under the pointer shows only the card hover.
- Respect Reduce Motion: replace movement and scaling with a simple fade.

## Look ("Deep water")
- Colors come only from the named tokens in `Theme.swift`. Never hard-code colors.
- Mode colors (surface): Dip `#9BE59A`, Dive `#2EC4D6`, Deep dive `#6F7CF2`; water: `#2F8A5C` / `#1A7686` / `#2E3F9A`. Modes must stay distinguishable by hue, not only lightness. Break uses the sand tokens.
- Base `#0E1A21`. Queue and LATER rows are rounded cards (`bgCard`, radius 10, 5 pt gaps). Done and History rows are flat.
- Timer digits: SF Pro Rounded. Everything else: SF Pro with monospaced digits.
- Primary actions are pills in the mode color. Secondary actions are text links.
- The tank's waves animate only while a session is running. They freeze while paused and stay still while idle, while the window isn't visible, or when Reduce Motion is on.
- The entire visible area of a control is clickable (`contentShape`). Hover area = click area.

## Performance
- Continuous decorative motion uses Core Animation transform animations, never per-frame redraws.
- Timer text and state are driven by the model tick, never by an animation.
- Persistence runs off the main thread, debounced; History is append-only.
- Every user action must update the UI within 100 ms, also with `dev.sh --seed-large`.

## Cursors (addition)
- All clickable controls use the shared pointing-hand style or modifier. `scripts/check-cursors.sh` must pass before finishing a task.

## Before you finish
- [ ] Cursor, hover, and disabled states correct on every touched control
- [ ] `scripts/check-cursors.sh` passes
- [ ] Tooltip and accessibility label on icon-only controls
- [ ] Checked at 450×550 and at the default size
- [ ] Checked with Reduce Motion on
- [ ] No double animations or flicker
- [ ] Icon-only buttons have a 28×28 square hit area and hover
- Tank colors come from one set derived from (phase, mode, paused) and update together: air, water body, back wave, crest, digits, pause glyph, text, scale. Fade the existing layers with explicit 400 ms `CABasicAnimation`s (none with Reduce Motion), never recreate them. Never freeze waves with `layer.speed = 0` or a `timeOffset`: it also freezes every other animation on that layer, including the color fade. Remove the slide animation and keep its offset as a static transform instead.
